  "result": "I fixed the cross-organization leak; I didn't run the tests.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts`, `findIssueById` looked issues up by id alone. It received the organization id as an argument but never used it in the query. The service layer (`getIssue` in `src/server/services/issue-service.ts`) does check that the user belongs to the organization in the request. But the database lookup then returned any issue with a matching id, whichever organization owned it.\n\n**Fix:** The query now filters by organization as well as by issue id, the same way the other lookups in that file already do. An issue from another organization now comes back as not found, so the service treats it as if it doesn't exist.\n\nThis one function is also used when updating an issue or changing its status, so those paths are covered by the same fix.",
